1
00:00:03,203 --> 00:00:05,138
Suture stump of remnant stomach. 4-0 silk.

2
00:00:08,008 --> 00:00:09,809
First assistant, hold over there.

3
00:00:10,043 --> 00:00:11,077
Tweezers.

4
00:00:12,612 --> 00:00:15,415
BP 105 over 72. Pulse 68.

5
00:00:15,482 --> 00:00:17,183
Hold steady.

6
00:00:18,351 --> 00:00:22,389
Do you know how to perform reconstructive
surgery after fundusectomy op?

7
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:25,658
Normally double tract.

8
00:00:26,393 --> 00:00:27,894
You're right.

9
00:00:28,128 --> 00:00:30,096
No. In this case,

10
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:32,699
there is an option called double-flap.

11
00:00:32,832 --> 00:00:35,635
Double-flap? No, no way.

12
00:00:35,702 --> 00:00:36,836
Double-flap.

13
00:00:36,903 --> 00:00:40,840
You're right! Ito, you got it!

14
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:44,210
Make a flap. A muscular incision
in H type. Monopolar.

15
00:00:49,783 --> 00:00:52,085
Hurry up and peel off the flap.

16
00:00:52,452 --> 00:00:54,521
I'm sorry. Pean.

17
00:00:56,656 --> 00:00:57,590
Don't pull too hard.

18
00:00:57,657 --> 00:00:59,692
- You're damaging the vascular plexus.
- Sorry.

19
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:02,962
BP dropped to 70. Pulse 55.

20
00:01:03,029 --> 00:01:03,863
Sorry.

21
00:01:06,966 --> 00:01:11,037
Vitals. BP 120 over 80.
Pulse 80, normal sinus rhythm.

22
00:01:11,337 --> 00:01:12,439
Done.

23
00:01:13,139 --> 00:01:14,040
Blood loss?

24
00:01:14,174 --> 00:01:15,208
150 cc.

25
00:01:19,579 --> 00:01:20,747
Thank you, doctor.

26
00:01:20,847 --> 00:01:21,981
Good job.

27
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:31,791
You guys are to gain experience
day by day, step by step, you know...

28
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:33,093
No!

29
00:01:42,202 --> 00:01:45,004
I'm so happy.

30
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:48,675
Michiko stop it. Look at your face.

31
00:01:48,808 --> 00:01:50,510
I can't help it. It's yummy.

32
00:01:50,643 --> 00:01:53,580
You don't know who's watching.

33
00:01:53,646 --> 00:01:55,682
It's okay. Okay. Okay.

34
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:57,217
Hot!

35
00:01:57,283 --> 00:02:01,387
I told you stop making that face.
You'll pay for it.

36
00:02:06,559 --> 00:02:07,694
Here I am.

37
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:10,830
You bathe too long.

38
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:13,133
Don't say that. I'm a girl.

39
00:02:13,199 --> 00:02:15,001
What about me?

40
00:02:20,273 --> 00:02:22,175
What's wrong?

41
00:02:23,243 --> 00:02:24,544
TAKOYAKI

42
00:02:25,345 --> 00:02:30,517
Akira, lend me $5, will you?

43
00:02:30,617 --> 00:02:32,318
What? $5?

44
00:02:32,385 --> 00:02:34,287
Whatever. Whatever. I'll be happy.

45
00:02:35,955 --> 00:02:37,590
Here you are.

46
00:02:37,657 --> 00:02:40,160
- Hot! Hot!
- Sit and eat.

47
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:43,163
- Here.
- Okay.

48
00:02:43,763 --> 00:02:45,064
I don't need this.

49
00:02:45,598 --> 00:02:46,533
What are you doing?

50
00:02:49,235 --> 00:02:50,937
You're exaggerating!

51
00:02:51,137 --> 00:02:52,705
Hot! Hot!

52
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:56,576
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

53
00:02:58,978 --> 00:03:00,713
- What did you say?
- Hey, hey.

54
00:03:01,047 --> 00:03:02,682
The four young surgeons. All of them?

55
00:03:02,815 --> 00:03:04,617
- They're not doing rounds.
- No?

56
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:05,885
Why?

57
00:03:05,952 --> 00:03:07,253
- It's inconvenient for them.
- What?

58
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:12,192
This is the director's rounds.
No one dares to say it's inconvenient.

59
00:03:12,258 --> 00:03:13,993
How about Deputy Chief Surgeon Torii?

60
00:03:14,494 --> 00:03:15,962
It's inconvenient for him, too?

61
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:18,064
He's attending a meeting in Yamanashi.

62
00:03:20,333 --> 00:03:23,937
So, he is skipping the director's rounds.
He's done for now.

63
00:03:24,070 --> 00:03:29,509
This is the director's rounds. I've never
heard of anyone being inconvenient.

64
00:03:29,576 --> 00:03:31,711
- Excuse me!
- Yes.

65
00:03:31,778 --> 00:03:33,413
Director Hiruma can't make it.

66
00:03:34,514 --> 00:03:36,049
- Why?
- It's inconvenient for him.

67
00:03:39,185 --> 00:03:40,420
Well, let's go.

68
00:03:41,354 --> 00:03:47,560
<i>In 2017, the once sacrosanct</i>
<i>university medical system</i>

69
00:03:51,664 --> 00:03:53,199
<i>finally collapsed.</i>

70
00:03:53,766 --> 00:03:58,871
Toxins that were crippling this hospital
have been completely purged.

71
00:03:58,972 --> 00:04:00,974
Clean is beautiful.

72
00:04:01,274 --> 00:04:06,512
<i>University hospitals launched a reform</i>
<i>to regain their true purpose.</i>

73
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:09,048
<i>But that was a wishful thinking.</i>

74
00:04:09,282 --> 00:04:10,116
Mistress?

75
00:04:10,183 --> 00:04:11,117
Kissing in his room.

76
00:04:11,184 --> 00:04:12,585
Highly unethical.

77
00:04:13,453 --> 00:04:15,622
We're longing for good steak.

78
00:04:16,022 --> 00:04:18,625
I can read between the lines.

79
00:04:19,292 --> 00:04:23,896
<i>The university medical system</i>
<i>regained its once-lost authority</i>

80
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:30,003
<i>and the system on which lives depend</i>
<i>strayed away from what it should be.</i>

81
00:04:30,069 --> 00:04:36,643
Under my leadership, we can bring
glory back to Totei University Hospital.

82
00:04:37,176 --> 00:04:38,177
Yes sir.

83
00:04:40,847 --> 00:04:45,518
<i>In the midst of reform, doctors free</i>
<i>from any establishment emerged.</i>

84
00:04:46,019 --> 00:04:49,989
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

85
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:53,293
This woman, for example.

86
00:04:54,727 --> 00:04:56,162
Here's soy sauce.

87
00:05:00,366 --> 00:05:04,304
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

88
00:05:04,837 --> 00:05:10,376
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

89
00:05:11,744 --> 00:05:14,614
You don't attend the director's rounds.

90
00:05:15,014 --> 00:05:16,316
I decline.

91
00:05:17,016 --> 00:05:19,852
So your contract is freelance.

92
00:05:20,053 --> 00:05:24,791
I decline everything that doesn't
require a medical license.

93
00:05:25,024 --> 00:05:26,359
The cliché.

94
00:05:26,626 --> 00:05:29,729
Chauffeur to golf courses.
Covering up extramarital affairs.

95
00:05:30,463 --> 00:05:33,099
I decline.

96
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:34,167
Be quiet.

97
00:05:36,302 --> 00:05:37,203
Dr. Daimon.

98
00:05:37,337 --> 00:05:39,405
About yesterday's operation.

99
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:45,311
Normally we do double tract
but you did double-flap, right?

100
00:05:45,712 --> 00:05:46,612
So?

101
00:05:46,813 --> 00:05:49,015
They didn't get why you did that.

102
00:05:49,248 --> 00:05:54,654
Your decision was to evade the risk
of reflux esophagitis.

103
00:05:56,222 --> 00:05:57,357
I agree.

104
00:05:57,857 --> 00:05:58,858
Thanks.

105
00:05:59,292 --> 00:06:02,261
I'm sure, I'll get along with you.

106
00:06:08,634 --> 00:06:11,337
Someone was over there...

107
00:06:13,005 --> 00:06:14,040
Yeah?

108
00:06:17,977 --> 00:06:20,213
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

109
00:06:20,747 --> 00:06:23,850
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

110
00:06:47,774 --> 00:06:49,242
This is for your own good.

111
00:06:50,510 --> 00:06:53,112
I can't do a detailed examination here.

112
00:06:53,179 --> 00:06:54,480
OKOSHI INTERNAL MEDICINE

113
00:06:54,547 --> 00:07:00,820
I recommend you go to
a big hospital with proper facilities.

114
00:07:01,687 --> 00:07:04,023
A big hospital.

115
00:07:11,831 --> 00:07:14,667
You better think more.

116
00:07:15,768 --> 00:07:16,736
About what?

117
00:07:16,903 --> 00:07:21,574
Merits of the director's round.
Better communication with patients.

118
00:07:21,674 --> 00:07:25,278
Gives you a chance to review
and practice your basic studies.

119
00:07:25,344 --> 00:07:26,546
Any problems?

120
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:32,618
We need to prepare our papers
and study the operation of the day...

121
00:07:32,985 --> 00:07:34,353
I think there is a priority.

122
00:07:36,022 --> 00:07:37,557
- Deputy Chief Surgeon.
- It's okay.

123
00:07:37,657 --> 00:07:41,961
Okay, then, what made you decide
to become a doctor?

124
00:07:42,028 --> 00:07:46,265
I want you to remember your
initial motivation, Arima.

125
00:07:46,332 --> 00:07:48,334
Why did you want to become a doctor?

126
00:07:48,668 --> 00:07:51,871
Because my parents are practitioners.

127
00:07:51,971 --> 00:07:52,805
Kurokawa?

128
00:07:52,972 --> 00:07:56,209
Med students are stars at college.
I guess, for a social status?!

129
00:07:56,275 --> 00:07:57,910
Ito. Hey!

130
00:07:59,011 --> 00:07:59,979
Sorry, wasn't listening.

131
00:08:00,046 --> 00:08:00,880
No, it's okay.

132
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:03,616
Nishiyama? What was your reason?

133
00:08:05,451 --> 00:08:06,652
How about you?

134
00:08:06,786 --> 00:08:07,854
Me?

135
00:08:08,254 --> 00:08:11,123
Well, I...

136
00:08:13,292 --> 00:08:14,193
Yes?

137
00:08:16,262 --> 00:08:17,363
Three...

138
00:08:17,430 --> 00:08:18,464
Two...

139
00:08:18,898 --> 00:08:19,899
One...

140
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:22,935
It's 5:00 p.m., time to go home.

141
00:08:25,738 --> 00:08:26,772
Me, too.

142
00:08:27,406 --> 00:08:28,541
See you.

143
00:08:28,608 --> 00:08:30,710
Hey. Wait. Wait.

144
00:08:30,810 --> 00:08:32,211
Don't copy her.

145
00:08:32,445 --> 00:08:34,313
Wait! Hey!

146
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:35,848
Dr. Hara, they won't listen.

147
00:08:36,716 --> 00:08:38,184
Bye.

148
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:43,055
See you.

149
00:08:45,958 --> 00:08:46,826
Hara.

150
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:48,895
Education. They need education.

151
00:08:49,662 --> 00:08:53,699
If we don't educate them there will be
no future health care in Japan.

152
00:08:53,866 --> 00:08:57,737
We must teach them what a doctor
is all about. Drum into their heads.

153
00:08:57,937 --> 00:08:59,739
It's in your head, right?

154
00:09:01,874 --> 00:09:02,942
No.

155
00:09:17,823 --> 00:09:18,991
Are you all right?

156
00:09:20,793 --> 00:09:21,661
Can I?

157
00:09:21,727 --> 00:09:24,463
I'm all right. I'm all right.

158
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:26,032
Mom?

159
00:09:28,367 --> 00:09:29,368
Ryoji.

160
00:09:30,336 --> 00:09:31,270
What's wrong?

161
00:09:32,772 --> 00:09:34,307
It's best she has a checkup.

162
00:09:34,607 --> 00:09:35,875
I'm fine.

163
00:09:35,942 --> 00:09:37,610
There's nothing wrong with me.

164
00:09:40,046 --> 00:09:42,415
Why are you here? I'm leaving.

165
00:09:42,682 --> 00:09:46,052
Why don't we have dinner together?

166
00:09:46,118 --> 00:09:47,620
I have plans.

167
00:09:48,454 --> 00:09:49,355
Hey.

168
00:09:50,623 --> 00:09:51,457
Hey!

169
00:09:52,391 --> 00:09:53,559
Excuse me.

170
00:09:54,827 --> 00:09:58,831
I'm fine. Nothing is wrong with me.
I appreciate your concern.

171
00:09:59,765 --> 00:10:01,601
Dr. Michiko Daimon.

172
00:10:07,573 --> 00:10:09,475
She knows me.

173
00:10:11,744 --> 00:10:14,347
They're typical
"pressure-free" generation.

174
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:15,615
Oh, I know.

175
00:10:16,248 --> 00:10:18,551
I'm pressure-free generation. What's up?

176
00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:20,987
What's that? Scary.

177
00:10:21,754 --> 00:10:25,091
"Riichi." What's up?

178
00:10:25,157 --> 00:10:26,592
Oh, my.

179
00:10:27,426 --> 00:10:30,796
By the way, Hiromi...

180
00:10:32,932 --> 00:10:35,234
I'm scared to walk at night by myself.

181
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:36,335
Why?

182
00:10:36,402 --> 00:10:37,570
Recently...

183
00:10:39,071 --> 00:10:41,474
She feels like someone is following her.

184
00:10:41,607 --> 00:10:42,541
Really?

185
00:10:43,309 --> 00:10:46,479
Somebody was hiding and
taking my pictures.

186
00:10:47,747 --> 00:10:49,482
It's a stalker.

187
00:10:49,649 --> 00:10:51,884
Stop it. No way.

188
00:10:51,951 --> 00:10:55,321
You don't look like a
divorcee with a child.

189
00:10:55,621 --> 00:10:58,691
Really? Do you think so?

190
00:10:58,758 --> 00:11:02,128
Too self-conscious, but what's up?

191
00:11:02,261 --> 00:11:05,097
Shut up! Ron!

192
00:11:05,231 --> 00:11:08,501
Me, too. Double ron.

193
00:11:08,601 --> 00:11:10,136
Here. Uradora.

194
00:11:34,126 --> 00:11:35,027
Well...

195
00:11:35,294 --> 00:11:37,129
What's the matter with you?

196
00:11:37,663 --> 00:11:39,198
Hm? Nothing.

197
00:11:39,398 --> 00:11:40,466
But...

198
00:11:41,133 --> 00:11:43,302
Glad to see you're fine.

199
00:11:43,536 --> 00:11:44,437
I'm glad.

200
00:11:45,671 --> 00:11:50,309
We were worried
because you cancelled the rounds.

201
00:11:51,510 --> 00:11:54,580
Yeah, I had something.

202
00:11:55,815 --> 00:11:57,950
By the way...

203
00:11:58,784 --> 00:12:02,855
recently I feel

204
00:12:04,290 --> 00:12:10,730
I'm being watched by someone.
Someone is targeting me.

205
00:12:11,530 --> 00:12:12,431
Maybe...

206
00:12:12,498 --> 00:12:13,733
It's just your imagination.

207
00:12:13,833 --> 00:12:14,867
Imagination?

208
00:12:14,934 --> 00:12:16,302
That's unpardonable!

209
00:12:16,368 --> 00:12:17,937
Who would do that?

210
00:12:18,003 --> 00:12:19,872
- Well...
- So it is...

211
00:12:19,939 --> 00:12:25,377
Yes, but I have a rough idea.

212
00:12:25,544 --> 00:12:27,279
Excuse me.

213
00:12:27,346 --> 00:12:28,280
Who's this?

214
00:12:28,481 --> 00:12:30,583
Please wait!

215
00:12:32,051 --> 00:12:34,520
I knew it.

216
00:12:34,854 --> 00:12:38,057
This is your first time meeting him.

217
00:12:38,290 --> 00:12:43,129
He is an auditor of Totei
University Hospital.

218
00:12:43,662 --> 00:12:44,730
Kijisawa.

219
00:12:45,131 --> 00:12:46,332
Our auditor?!

220
00:12:46,532 --> 00:12:49,201
Nice to meet you. I'm Shinnosuke Kijisawa.

221
00:12:49,435 --> 00:12:52,838
Under the order from Chairman Uchikanda,
of Japan Doctors Club

222
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:58,010
I'll be coming here as an auditor
on an irregular basis.

223
00:12:58,110 --> 00:12:58,944
Irregular basis.

224
00:12:59,211 --> 00:13:01,113
In other words...

225
00:13:02,681 --> 00:13:04,049
A surprise inspection.

226
00:13:04,817 --> 00:13:06,886
A surprise inspection?

227
00:13:07,119 --> 00:13:11,423
What kind of inspection will you do today?

228
00:13:11,590 --> 00:13:14,727
To start with, I visited various locations

229
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:16,862
- in this hospital.
- In this hospital.

230
00:13:16,929 --> 00:13:22,802
First, the Surgery Department Office is
very messy.

231
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:29,375
A messy work environment symbolizes
a messy mentality of the workers there.

232
00:13:31,877 --> 00:13:32,978
That stupid woman.

233
00:13:34,013 --> 00:13:37,516
Michiko Daimon is a freelance...

234
00:13:37,616 --> 00:13:42,655
University hospitals are the symbol of
Japan's medical industry.

235
00:13:43,189 --> 00:13:44,056
You're right.

236
00:13:44,123 --> 00:13:49,628
As an exceptional measure, you
are here to rebuild our organization.

237
00:13:49,962 --> 00:13:54,133
To have you back as the director is
indeed a very exceptional measure.

238
00:13:54,567 --> 00:13:55,501
And yet

239
00:13:56,268 --> 00:13:58,070
what a wretched state you are in.

240
00:13:59,438 --> 00:14:05,644
My words are Chairman Uchikanda's words.

241
00:14:05,711 --> 00:14:06,712
Be prepared.

242
00:14:06,812 --> 00:14:07,646
Yes sir.

243
00:14:07,813 --> 00:14:13,085
From now on,
I demand a thorough compliance.

244
00:14:13,252 --> 00:14:18,224
I'll be deadly strict on checking
the flow of money.

245
00:14:18,891 --> 00:14:20,025
Yes, I'm sure you'll do it well.

246
00:14:21,193 --> 00:14:24,063
Director Hiruma!

247
00:14:24,730 --> 00:14:27,233
Please don't.

248
00:14:27,466 --> 00:14:28,801
It's me.

249
00:14:28,901 --> 00:14:32,905
Thank you for taking care of my son.

250
00:14:33,205 --> 00:14:34,139
Your son?

251
00:14:34,273 --> 00:14:40,212
My son is assigned to the Surgery
Department Office. I'm Ryoji Ito's mother.

252
00:14:40,346 --> 00:14:44,016
Ito? Who?

253
00:14:44,083 --> 00:14:47,720
Ito! One of the four young surgeons.
Ito's mother?

254
00:14:47,853 --> 00:14:49,355
I'm his mother.

255
00:14:49,488 --> 00:14:51,090
I see. Nice to meet you.

256
00:14:51,190 --> 00:14:53,826
Why did you come here?

257
00:14:54,159 --> 00:15:00,599
From now on, Ryoji will start to
train to become a fully qualified doctor.

258
00:15:00,699 --> 00:15:07,573
I wanted to pay my courtesy call
on Director Hiruma in person.

259
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:10,042
That is very thoughtful.

260
00:15:10,109 --> 00:15:12,878
Thank you for your generous

261
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:17,616
support toward Ryoji.

262
00:15:18,918 --> 00:15:21,320
- I don't know...
- Excuse me.

263
00:15:22,988 --> 00:15:24,023
Sweets.

264
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:29,194
What's this?

265
00:15:29,261 --> 00:15:30,796
These are sweets.

266
00:15:31,864 --> 00:15:32,765
You're rude!

267
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:39,104
Are you trying to make a mockery of us?

268
00:15:39,738 --> 00:15:43,542
No, it is just my appreciation.

269
00:15:43,642 --> 00:15:49,682
A thing like this! Director Hiruma
will never accept it.

270
00:15:49,782 --> 00:15:50,749
I can't accept this.

271
00:15:50,849 --> 00:15:52,217
- Get out!
- I can't accept it.

272
00:15:52,284 --> 00:15:53,218
Go!

273
00:15:57,122 --> 00:15:59,391
I'm sorry.

274
00:16:02,494 --> 00:16:03,395
Ebina.

275
00:16:03,529 --> 00:16:05,698
Give this back to her.

276
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:07,366
I'll give it back.

277
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:09,969
And I mean...

278
00:16:10,102 --> 00:16:10,936
Yes sir.

279
00:16:11,670 --> 00:16:12,838
This is disgraceful.

280
00:16:14,773 --> 00:16:16,308
First time to see anything like that.

281
00:16:16,408 --> 00:16:18,644
Yeah, I was just shocked.

282
00:16:18,711 --> 00:16:20,913
- First time?
- I'm scared.

283
00:16:22,114 --> 00:16:23,782
Ito's mother?

284
00:16:26,585 --> 00:16:27,920
Ms. Ito?

285
00:16:29,355 --> 00:16:30,389
Where are you?

286
00:16:31,857 --> 00:16:33,759
No, I don't mean to...

287
00:16:33,859 --> 00:16:37,496
No, I'm not...

288
00:16:42,401 --> 00:16:43,836
Where is she?

289
00:16:50,509 --> 00:16:51,677
Ms. Ito!

290
00:16:52,411 --> 00:16:55,547
Ms. Ito! Good. Good.

291
00:16:55,814 --> 00:17:02,287
About the sweets. I'll return this
and take that. Is that OK?

292
00:17:03,088 --> 00:17:04,056
Ms. Ito?

293
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:10,829
Are you okay?

294
00:17:11,296 --> 00:17:12,197
Ms. Ito!

295
00:17:13,599 --> 00:17:15,701
Ms. Ito, are you okay?

296
00:17:16,201 --> 00:17:18,804
Hang in there.

297
00:17:19,605 --> 00:17:22,274
Are you all right?

298
00:17:23,675 --> 00:17:25,911
Pull yourself together.

299
00:17:27,579 --> 00:17:30,382
Hey, are you okay?

300
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:34,053
Somebody bring a stretcher!
Vomiting blood!

301
00:17:35,988 --> 00:17:37,456
Dr. Ebina.

302
00:17:38,524 --> 00:17:41,193
I told them to go to the Endoscopy Center.

303
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:42,828
Did you get in touch with Ito?

304
00:17:43,095 --> 00:17:45,464
He turned in a notice for
early leave today.

305
00:17:45,564 --> 00:17:46,832
Early leave?

306
00:17:46,932 --> 00:17:48,767
He's going to his friend's live.

307
00:17:49,468 --> 00:17:51,503
- Live?
- Live as in a live concert?

308
00:17:51,570 --> 00:17:52,805
Yes, like this.

309
00:17:53,138 --> 00:17:56,909
His mother is in bad condition.
He should be more responsible as a doctor.

310
00:17:57,142 --> 00:18:02,181
What're you holding?

311
00:18:02,247 --> 00:18:03,982
- Sweets.
- Sweets?

312
00:18:04,049 --> 00:18:07,319
Forget it.
Just go to the Endoscopy Center!

313
00:18:07,886 --> 00:18:08,987
Excuse me.

314
00:18:09,054 --> 00:18:10,489
I got this for you.

315
00:18:13,859 --> 00:18:14,893
How should I open it?

316
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:17,596
Just open it.

317
00:18:20,399 --> 00:18:21,333
Sorry.

318
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:22,468
You...

319
00:18:22,568 --> 00:18:23,535
I'm sorry.

320
00:18:24,903 --> 00:18:29,508
Thank God. I was worried.

321
00:18:29,575 --> 00:18:32,711
Ito's mother was...

322
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:34,046
Fell down.

323
00:18:35,214 --> 00:18:36,548
I'm worried.

324
00:18:36,915 --> 00:18:39,952
You should do as much as you can for her.

325
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:45,591
Her thoughtfulness is pretty rare
these days.

326
00:18:45,891 --> 00:18:46,892
Yes sir.

327
00:18:47,059 --> 00:18:51,697
Of the four young surgeons,
you look out for Ito.

328
00:18:52,097 --> 00:18:56,001
Raise him to be a good surgeon.

329
00:18:56,702 --> 00:18:58,804
As his boss, he is your responsibility.

330
00:19:00,372 --> 00:19:01,373
My responsibility?

331
00:19:01,473 --> 00:19:02,708
Yes, your responsibility.

332
00:19:04,042 --> 00:19:04,877
Yes sir.

333
00:19:05,444 --> 00:19:07,746
However

334
00:19:08,514 --> 00:19:11,283
do not let Michiko Daimon meddle in this.

335
00:19:12,417 --> 00:19:13,485
Yes sir.

336
00:19:14,953 --> 00:19:17,756
"Yes sir"?
How could you say that?

337
00:19:18,624 --> 00:19:22,494
How many times have you betrayed me?

338
00:19:22,561 --> 00:19:23,662
I've never betrayed you.

339
00:19:34,006 --> 00:19:36,308
Right there. Go deeper.

340
00:19:36,675 --> 00:19:38,210
Hey, Daimon. What are you doing?

341
00:19:38,277 --> 00:19:40,379
There's suspicion of
the duodenal invasion.

342
00:19:41,146 --> 00:19:42,047
Change the angle.

343
00:19:42,314 --> 00:19:45,584
Hara, just find Ito and
call him back here!

344
00:19:45,684 --> 00:19:48,820
He doesn't answer his phone or
reply to my emails.

345
00:19:49,021 --> 00:19:50,155
Where did he go?

346
00:19:50,289 --> 00:19:52,257
I don't know.

347
00:19:52,324 --> 00:19:54,092
- Be quiet.
- Sorry.

348
00:19:54,459 --> 00:19:56,328
Daimon, move.

349
00:19:56,395 --> 00:19:58,497
- She is my patient.
- I decline.

350
00:19:58,564 --> 00:19:59,865
Ito reports directly to me.

351
00:19:59,932 --> 00:20:01,133
- She is his mother.
- So?

352
00:20:01,266 --> 00:20:04,203
So as his boss, I'm responsible
for her treatment.

353
00:20:04,803 --> 00:20:08,040
My words are Director Hiruma's words.

354
00:20:08,207 --> 00:20:09,908
I decline even more.

355
00:20:11,343 --> 00:20:12,711
Please.

356
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:17,115
It might be a troublesome case.

357
00:20:17,849 --> 00:20:19,251
It could be a carcinosarcoma.

358
00:20:22,821 --> 00:20:24,022
A cancer sarcoma?

359
00:20:27,593 --> 00:20:31,697
This patient is 55 years old,
female. Fujiko Ito.

360
00:20:32,431 --> 00:20:36,635
As a result of the endoscopic biopsy,
a mix of cancer and sarcoma was observed.

361
00:20:39,171 --> 00:20:43,242
Advanced gallbladder
carcinosarcoma, stage 3.

362
00:20:43,742 --> 00:20:47,346
A 5 cm tumor developed from
the gallbladder neck to the bile duct.

363
00:20:47,746 --> 00:20:49,615
It also entered the hepatic portal area.

364
00:20:50,682 --> 00:20:51,783
Not good.

365
00:20:52,117 --> 00:20:52,951
No.

366
00:20:53,118 --> 00:20:57,055
Carcinosarcoma of the gallbladder is
extremely rare and unfavorable.

367
00:20:58,824 --> 00:21:02,995
Your mom, right?
Why didn't you know that?

368
00:21:04,229 --> 00:21:06,665
We don't live together.

369
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,034
Okay.

370
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:11,403
The operation plan is

371
00:21:11,803 --> 00:21:16,975
extended right lobectomy with
extrahepatic bile duct resection.

372
00:21:20,212 --> 00:21:24,950
If this method is used,
radical resection is possible.

373
00:21:25,050 --> 00:21:25,951
Objection.

374
00:21:27,819 --> 00:21:31,256
When the duodenal bile duct stump
becomes cancer positive

375
00:21:31,356 --> 00:21:32,491
it can't be radically resected.

376
00:21:33,258 --> 00:21:34,826
I mean...

377
00:21:38,730 --> 00:21:39,564
Sir.

378
00:21:39,865 --> 00:21:44,469
I know she is your mom so you can
get out of the operation this time.

379
00:21:44,536 --> 00:21:45,904
No, not like that.

380
00:21:46,371 --> 00:21:47,205
What?

381
00:21:47,506 --> 00:21:48,807
The patient...

382
00:21:48,874 --> 00:21:49,941
The patient?

383
00:21:50,309 --> 00:21:54,346
There is a possibility of duodenal
invasion by ultrasonic endoscopy.

384
00:21:54,746 --> 00:21:56,415
Dr. Daimon is right.

385
00:21:57,816 --> 00:21:58,717
I mean...

386
00:21:59,017 --> 00:22:01,787
How about simultaneous resection of
the hepatopancreatic duodenum?

387
00:22:02,554 --> 00:22:04,323
Simultaneous resection of
the hepatopancreatic duodenum?

388
00:22:04,656 --> 00:22:09,061
In addition to removing the gallbladder,
bile duct and right lobe of liver

389
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:12,698
remove all from the pancreas head and
the stomach pylorus to the duodenum.

390
00:22:13,598 --> 00:22:17,836
This method can cure the tumor completely.

391
00:22:20,272 --> 00:22:24,042
Good. You studied a lot.

392
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:26,545
No objection.

393
00:22:28,747 --> 00:22:30,916
Let's do it.

394
00:22:31,049 --> 00:22:31,983
Wait a minute.

395
00:22:32,117 --> 00:22:35,220
I get along with Dr. Daimon.

396
00:22:37,556 --> 00:22:38,657
There is one problem.

397
00:22:39,257 --> 00:22:40,092
What?

398
00:22:40,859 --> 00:22:44,096
I think this operation is
difficult for Dr. Ebina.

399
00:22:46,598 --> 00:22:49,267
No objection. I can do it.

400
00:22:49,735 --> 00:22:52,738
But you're a part-timer.

401
00:22:53,405 --> 00:22:54,272
Hey.

402
00:22:58,677 --> 00:23:04,349
Well done. Ito is great.
He studied very hard.

403
00:23:05,484 --> 00:23:06,451
Right? Part-timer.

404
00:23:06,852 --> 00:23:08,353
Good job, Ito.

405
00:23:18,563 --> 00:23:19,765
Take a seat.

406
00:23:24,536 --> 00:23:27,105
Ito's proposal is great.

407
00:23:27,339 --> 00:23:32,310
Simultaneous resection of the
hepatopancreatic duodenum.

408
00:23:32,611 --> 00:23:34,646
But...

409
00:23:35,313 --> 00:23:36,214
Isn't it great?

410
00:23:37,849 --> 00:23:38,884
Yes, it is.

411
00:23:39,151 --> 00:23:39,985
Ito.

412
00:23:40,719 --> 00:23:41,753
Yes.

413
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:43,555
You must perform the surgery.

414
00:23:47,926 --> 00:23:50,362
To save your mother's life.

415
00:23:50,796 --> 00:23:53,632
Her son, a young surgeon,

416
00:23:54,866 --> 00:23:56,234
tackles the challenging operation.

417
00:23:56,868 --> 00:24:01,873
It is a very challenging surgery.

418
00:24:03,108 --> 00:24:04,342
It's impressive.

419
00:24:06,244 --> 00:24:12,117
According to the research,
Ito will be the youngest person

420
00:24:12,217 --> 00:24:15,754
in the world to perform the surgery.

421
00:24:15,887 --> 00:24:16,788
25-30 YEARS OLD: 0

422
00:24:16,855 --> 00:24:17,689
Awesome.

423
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:24,729
But this is...

424
00:24:25,797 --> 00:24:26,631
Reckless.

425
00:24:26,765 --> 00:24:27,666
What?

426
00:24:35,273 --> 00:24:40,745
This is an order from me as the director

427
00:24:41,379 --> 00:24:43,215
of the Totei University Hospital.

428
00:24:45,183 --> 00:24:46,852
- Ito is fine.
- Okay?

429
00:24:47,052 --> 00:24:49,454
I thought Ito was good
from the beginning.

430
00:24:49,554 --> 00:24:50,489
Obviously.

431
00:24:51,523 --> 00:24:53,758
Ito! Do your best!

432
00:24:54,025 --> 00:24:55,527
Just do it, Ito.

433
00:24:55,594 --> 00:24:56,528
Great!

434
00:24:56,595 --> 00:24:57,829
Do it.

435
00:24:58,630 --> 00:25:01,032
Ito, banzai!

436
00:25:01,166 --> 00:25:03,101
INFORMED CONSENT

437
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:05,570
Please sign the consent form.

438
00:25:09,674 --> 00:25:10,809
I decline.

439
00:25:12,210 --> 00:25:16,147
From the beginning, I didn't
plan to have any surgery.

440
00:25:16,348 --> 00:25:17,782
Really?

441
00:25:18,283 --> 00:25:19,851
I've decided already.

442
00:25:22,888 --> 00:25:23,722
Ito.

443
00:25:27,025 --> 00:25:30,629
She said so. There's nothing I can do.

444
00:25:32,898 --> 00:25:36,268
Are you really a doctor? Her son?

445
00:25:36,501 --> 00:25:42,440
We respect the intention of the patient.
I've learned that's the informed consent.

446
00:25:42,641 --> 00:25:43,842
He is right.

447
00:25:46,378 --> 00:25:49,714
Anyway I won't have the surgery.

448
00:25:51,683 --> 00:25:53,218
You'll die without surgery.

449
00:25:55,954 --> 00:25:58,089
The progression is fast.

450
00:25:58,423 --> 00:26:01,927
If you don't have the operation,
you'll die.

451
00:26:01,993 --> 00:26:03,161
Stop it.

452
00:26:04,095 --> 00:26:08,600
To force surgery without the patient's
consent is a compliance violation.

453
00:26:08,767 --> 00:26:10,001
Are you stupid?

454
00:26:12,103 --> 00:26:13,471
Excuse me.

455
00:26:19,477 --> 00:26:20,946
But Ms. Ito...

456
00:26:21,046 --> 00:26:22,113
Dr. Ebina.

457
00:26:26,585 --> 00:26:27,886
I must ask you to leave.

458
00:26:31,489 --> 00:26:33,158
Please, leave.

459
00:26:38,863 --> 00:26:40,632
I won't give up.

460
00:26:56,181 --> 00:26:59,184
That mother and son,
what the hell are they?

461
00:27:01,353 --> 00:27:02,420
Dr. Ebina.

462
00:27:03,221 --> 00:27:06,858
This was under the seat in the lobby.

463
00:27:07,058 --> 00:27:09,060
Take it to the lost and found.

464
00:27:09,227 --> 00:27:13,765
I was going to but
I saw a couple of pictures...

465
00:27:14,633 --> 00:27:15,567
and then...

466
00:27:26,511 --> 00:27:27,879
Oh my God.

467
00:27:31,449 --> 00:27:32,751
Oh, no.

468
00:28:03,815 --> 00:28:05,650
I told you I won't give up.

469
00:28:12,057 --> 00:28:13,792
Can I ask you a question?

470
00:28:15,627 --> 00:28:17,996
How did you know about me
when I first met you?

471
00:28:22,534 --> 00:28:24,069
What do you want to tell me?

472
00:28:24,369 --> 00:28:26,371
Auditor Kijisawa...

473
00:28:27,872 --> 00:28:31,910
You're such a shameless person.

474
00:28:32,977 --> 00:28:35,380
Shame on you.

475
00:28:37,816 --> 00:28:38,650
What's this?

476
00:28:39,751 --> 00:28:42,120
You dropped the digital camera, right?

477
00:28:42,253 --> 00:28:44,522
This was under the seat in the lobby.

478
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:50,462
You took these spy photos.

479
00:28:51,129 --> 00:28:53,832
You were talking about compliance.

480
00:28:54,566 --> 00:28:57,001
You sounded so serious.

481
00:28:59,337 --> 00:29:01,339
Don't get cocky.

482
00:29:01,439 --> 00:29:02,407
I'm sorry.

483
00:29:05,009 --> 00:29:09,047
You can't talk anything about compliance.

484
00:29:09,547 --> 00:29:11,116
Such a thing.

485
00:29:11,382 --> 00:29:14,552
It all depends on how you take it.

486
00:29:15,153 --> 00:29:17,989
This is not mine.

487
00:29:18,089 --> 00:29:20,058
You act so innocent.

488
00:29:21,926 --> 00:29:24,062
Now I know whose camera this is.

489
00:29:33,972 --> 00:29:35,440
I didn't notice this video.

490
00:29:37,242 --> 00:29:38,209
What's this?

491
00:29:42,147 --> 00:29:43,515
Congratulations.

492
00:29:45,316 --> 00:29:52,056
My son will become a surgeon at Totei
University Hospital from this spring!

493
00:29:54,993 --> 00:29:57,896
Why did she do such a thing?

494
00:30:00,799 --> 00:30:01,666
Ebina.

495
00:30:02,300 --> 00:30:03,234
Yes.

496
00:30:03,635 --> 00:30:04,602
I got

497
00:30:06,971 --> 00:30:09,307
a brilliant idea.

498
00:30:11,276 --> 00:30:12,343
Voyeur?

499
00:30:16,347 --> 00:30:18,416
What are you up to?

500
00:30:18,716 --> 00:30:21,152
I apologize.

501
00:30:21,719 --> 00:30:27,592
But I wanted to know about the patients
and people who work here.

502
00:30:32,263 --> 00:30:33,531
For your son's sake?

503
00:30:34,532 --> 00:30:38,036
Because he works here.

504
00:30:38,803 --> 00:30:42,774
Good or bad as his co-worker.

505
00:30:43,441 --> 00:30:45,510
I thought better to check it out.

506
00:30:48,513 --> 00:30:49,747
Dr. Daimon.

507
00:30:50,782 --> 00:30:54,352
I know how my condition is.

508
00:30:55,653 --> 00:30:59,157
Even if I have an operation,
it's too late.

509
00:30:59,791 --> 00:31:05,396
The hospital that my son works for
couldn't cure his mother.

510
00:31:06,097 --> 00:31:11,035
I don't want to leave a stain
on his future.

511
00:31:13,404 --> 00:31:19,177
If I must die, I'd rather die at another
hospital unrelated to my son.

512
00:31:22,013 --> 00:31:23,815
Everything is for your son's sake.

513
00:31:26,284 --> 00:31:28,887
So your son won't crash or fall.

514
00:31:28,953 --> 00:31:29,921
Yes.

515
00:31:30,521 --> 00:31:33,625
You don't want him to have
a hard time.

516
00:31:33,858 --> 00:31:36,227
It's natural because I'm his mother.

517
00:31:36,294 --> 00:31:37,428
In a word,

518
00:31:38,863 --> 00:31:43,101
you don't believe in your own son.

519
00:31:46,170 --> 00:31:47,472
Even though you're his mother.

520
00:31:55,079 --> 00:31:57,949
What're you doing?
The nurses are looking for you.

521
00:31:58,016 --> 00:31:58,883
Ryoji.

522
00:32:00,251 --> 00:32:01,786
You're really annoying.

523
00:32:01,853 --> 00:32:04,055
I'm sorry...

524
00:32:08,559 --> 00:32:09,427
Sit down.

525
00:32:09,494 --> 00:32:10,495
Lie down sideways.

526
00:32:11,262 --> 00:32:12,363
Rub her back!

527
00:32:12,931 --> 00:32:13,831
Yes.

528
00:32:15,733 --> 00:32:17,035
What're you going to do?

529
00:32:18,136 --> 00:32:19,337
You are her surgeon.

530
00:32:21,105 --> 00:32:24,242
She didn't sign the consent form.
Too bad.

531
00:32:25,743 --> 00:32:26,878
Too bad?

532
00:32:27,812 --> 00:32:29,147
You're relieved, right?

533
00:32:43,328 --> 00:32:44,329
I won't give up.

534
00:33:25,970 --> 00:33:28,606
Daimon, would you excuse us?

535
00:33:31,109 --> 00:33:32,076
Please.

536
00:33:37,615 --> 00:33:38,616
You guys, too.

537
00:33:47,425 --> 00:33:48,292
What?

538
00:33:50,094 --> 00:33:51,095
Well.

539
00:33:53,731 --> 00:33:54,866
This is

540
00:33:55,700 --> 00:33:56,834
your camera, right?

541
00:34:00,304 --> 00:34:03,241
Many spy photos of people who work here.

542
00:34:03,908 --> 00:34:05,643
I don't know why but

543
00:34:06,978 --> 00:34:11,849
I can sue you as a crime.

544
00:34:17,054 --> 00:34:18,089
And...

545
00:34:19,557 --> 00:34:24,328
There's a case of you personally
handing cash over to the director.

546
00:34:28,066 --> 00:34:30,501
If the mother did such
criminal acts...

547
00:34:32,170 --> 00:34:35,973
Maybe your son can't
work here anymore.

548
00:34:39,844 --> 00:34:41,946
Well, I mean...

549
00:34:43,614 --> 00:34:45,049
My boss said so.

550
00:34:47,718 --> 00:34:48,786
Then...

551
00:34:50,088 --> 00:34:53,891
If you sign here
I can manage it somehow.

552
00:34:54,425 --> 00:34:56,527
This is a consent form.

553
00:35:02,266 --> 00:35:03,267
Excuse me.

554
00:35:07,805 --> 00:35:08,673
Here you are.

555
00:35:37,335 --> 00:35:39,971
I decline work that doesn't
require a medical license.

556
00:35:42,106 --> 00:35:43,407
I want to say that, too.

557
00:35:51,215 --> 00:35:53,751
INFORMED CONSENT

558
00:35:53,885 --> 00:35:56,187
FUJIKO ITO

559
00:36:00,691 --> 00:36:02,126
Freelancers are free-minded.

560
00:36:07,932 --> 00:36:09,066
I'm not being sarcastic.

561
00:36:33,591 --> 00:36:35,326
She signed it.

562
00:36:39,263 --> 00:36:40,364
Tomorrow is the surgery.

563
00:36:42,233 --> 00:36:43,401
You're her surgeon.

564
00:36:45,670 --> 00:36:47,071
If you have no confidence, say so.

565
00:36:48,039 --> 00:36:49,507
If you can't do it, just say so.

566
00:36:51,509 --> 00:36:52,743
Of course I'll do it.

567
00:36:54,979 --> 00:36:56,280
It'll be a hard operation.

568
00:36:58,015 --> 00:36:59,116
You need to be prepared.

569
00:36:59,550 --> 00:37:00,484
I know.

570
00:37:03,621 --> 00:37:04,789
Hey.

571
00:37:08,526 --> 00:37:12,396
To be stubborn and mentally prepared
are totally different.

572
00:37:18,669 --> 00:37:19,570
Don't worry.

573
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:22,373
I'll be your assistant.

574
00:37:28,846 --> 00:37:29,680
What's wrong?

575
00:37:31,415 --> 00:37:34,986
I'd like Dr. Daimon to assist me.

576
00:37:50,034 --> 00:37:53,237
The omentum is dissected at the
transverse colon attachment.

577
00:37:53,838 --> 00:37:56,307
Taping superior mesenteric vein.

578
00:37:59,243 --> 00:38:01,045
Order of homograft and rapid diagnosis.

579
00:38:01,112 --> 00:38:03,214
- Okay?
- Yes.

580
00:38:03,281 --> 00:38:04,415
What's the range of liver resection?

581
00:38:04,482 --> 00:38:06,550
Caudate lobe?
Gastrointestinal reconstruction?

582
00:38:07,385 --> 00:38:10,488
Extended right lobectomy
with total caudate lobe excision.

583
00:38:10,588 --> 00:38:12,790
Reconstruction is Roux-en-Y.

584
00:38:17,895 --> 00:38:20,898
We'll do our best and
back you up as your assistants.

585
00:38:20,998 --> 00:38:23,601
I know your future depends on this.

586
00:38:33,811 --> 00:38:36,447
OPERATING

587
00:38:38,049 --> 00:38:39,817
Vital is stable.

588
00:38:45,323 --> 00:38:48,259
Simultaneous resection of
the hepatopancreatic duodenum.

589
00:38:48,459 --> 00:38:49,560
Let's begin.

590
00:38:49,694 --> 00:38:51,228
Yes.

591
00:38:51,362 --> 00:38:52,196
Scalpel.

592
00:38:59,136 --> 00:39:01,772
Prepare for echo. The smallest probe.

593
00:39:02,273 --> 00:39:03,574
- Yes.
- Okay.

594
00:39:06,944 --> 00:39:08,079
Monopolar.

595
00:39:09,447 --> 00:39:10,314
Tweezers.

596
00:39:19,790 --> 00:39:22,126
He is lucky.

597
00:39:22,226 --> 00:39:24,428
He has something special.

598
00:39:24,829 --> 00:39:26,263
He is a step ahead.

599
00:39:26,630 --> 00:39:31,669
Since his mom's been here, he's been
studying hard and getting little sleep.

600
00:39:31,736 --> 00:39:32,837
I see.

601
00:39:33,571 --> 00:39:34,939
No surprise.

602
00:39:40,845 --> 00:39:41,679
Started?

603
00:39:41,812 --> 00:39:42,813
Just now.

604
00:39:45,015 --> 00:39:46,617
Is he okay?

605
00:39:47,218 --> 00:39:49,653
Yes. Because Michiko Daimon is
his assistant.

606
00:39:50,020 --> 00:39:51,589
Daimon again, huh.

607
00:39:59,897 --> 00:40:03,167
First, subtotal stomach-preserving
pancreaticoduodenectomy.

608
00:40:03,267 --> 00:40:04,201
Metzen.

609
00:40:18,783 --> 00:40:21,786
SURGERY TIME

610
00:40:28,325 --> 00:40:29,427
Compression of hemostasis, gauze.

611
00:40:29,527 --> 00:40:30,494
Suction.

612
00:40:33,464 --> 00:40:35,065
BP dropped to 70.

613
00:40:35,733 --> 00:40:36,767
What's this bleeding?

614
00:40:38,035 --> 00:40:40,070
Surgeon, look for a bleeding point.

615
00:40:40,171 --> 00:40:41,305
Sorry.

616
00:40:43,641 --> 00:40:48,045
BP below 60. Pulse 130.
RBC 10 units. ASAP!

617
00:40:48,179 --> 00:40:49,747
- Hurry.
- I know.

618
00:40:49,814 --> 00:40:52,183
If this goes on, hemorrhagic shock
and multiple organ failure...

619
00:40:52,616 --> 00:40:54,118
I can't find it anywhere.

620
00:40:54,852 --> 00:40:56,220
Daimon. What should we do?

621
00:40:59,423 --> 00:41:00,591
You know, right?

622
00:41:16,340 --> 00:41:17,408
In this case...

623
00:41:19,743 --> 00:41:21,212
Temporarily, stop the heart.

624
00:41:25,649 --> 00:41:26,550
You knew it.

625
00:41:29,019 --> 00:41:30,855
Not good.

626
00:41:30,955 --> 00:41:32,790
Stop her heart?

627
00:41:35,693 --> 00:41:38,362
Temporary cardiac arrest
by ATP administration.

628
00:41:38,462 --> 00:41:41,465
Stop the bleeding, find
the damaged part and restore it.

629
00:41:42,833 --> 00:41:44,168
We have a minute and a half.

630
00:41:44,602 --> 00:41:47,037
It's not enough.

631
00:41:47,505 --> 00:41:48,772
Impossible.

632
00:41:55,746 --> 00:41:58,148
Are you mentally prepared?

633
00:42:15,599 --> 00:42:18,969
Administer ATP. Stop her heart.

634
00:42:22,206 --> 00:42:24,008
Administer ATP.

635
00:42:34,919 --> 00:42:35,986
Cardiopulmonary arrest.

636
00:42:37,187 --> 00:42:38,589
Where's the damaged part?

637
00:42:49,700 --> 00:42:51,902
Where?

638
00:42:53,904 --> 00:42:56,307
ROSC in one minute.

639
00:42:57,641 --> 00:42:58,709
Tupfer.

640
00:43:07,885 --> 00:43:08,852
Move!

641
00:43:09,119 --> 00:43:10,421
Pass me a tupfer.

642
00:43:16,894 --> 00:43:18,095
40 seconds.

643
00:43:19,997 --> 00:43:23,734
This is unexpected. My proposal was...

644
00:43:23,801 --> 00:43:24,668
Shut up!

645
00:43:24,735 --> 00:43:25,703
30 seconds.

646
00:43:26,270 --> 00:43:27,237
But...

647
00:43:27,338 --> 00:43:29,139
I never fail.

648
00:43:33,310 --> 00:43:36,480
Here. Confirm bleeding point
in inferior vena cava.

649
00:43:36,714 --> 00:43:37,548
15 seconds.

650
00:43:37,748 --> 00:43:39,149
5-0 polypropylene.

651
00:43:39,216 --> 00:43:40,684
Hurry up.

652
00:43:48,058 --> 00:43:49,159
Fast.

653
00:43:49,326 --> 00:43:50,794
Cooper.

654
00:43:52,496 --> 00:43:53,964
Damaged part repaired.

655
00:44:01,739 --> 00:44:03,374
ROSC.

656
00:44:14,885 --> 00:44:16,754
Continue pancreaticoduodenectomy.

657
00:44:16,820 --> 00:44:18,255
Then right lobectomy.

658
00:44:18,322 --> 00:44:19,223
Hurry.

659
00:44:19,289 --> 00:44:20,357
Metzen.

660
00:44:39,810 --> 00:44:41,545
Finished. Blood loss?

661
00:44:41,745 --> 00:44:46,116
1,800 cc. BP 112 over 74,
normal sinus rhythm.

662
00:45:06,470 --> 00:45:07,471
Good job.

663
00:45:07,938 --> 00:45:09,339
Good job, doctor.

664
00:45:22,052 --> 00:45:24,722
Single parent?

665
00:45:26,523 --> 00:45:28,726
My father had an accident
right after I was born.

666
00:45:29,526 --> 00:45:30,461
I see.

667
00:45:31,428 --> 00:45:35,132
I was also raised only by my mother.

668
00:45:37,167 --> 00:45:38,368
I gave her a lot of trouble.

669
00:45:39,236 --> 00:45:40,738
I studied desperately.

670
00:45:40,804 --> 00:45:43,140
And I went to
Totei University then became a doctor.

671
00:45:43,874 --> 00:45:48,178
I just wanted her to feel
proud of me.

672
00:45:51,115 --> 00:45:52,583
Awesome.

673
00:45:53,016 --> 00:45:54,785
You, too.

674
00:45:56,987 --> 00:46:01,458
Actually, first, I went to
a third-rate university.

675
00:46:02,559 --> 00:46:03,560
Wasn't Totei?

676
00:46:05,095 --> 00:46:07,998
But it was a backdoor admission.

677
00:46:09,133 --> 00:46:09,967
A backdoor?!

678
00:46:10,868 --> 00:46:13,971
My mother's family had
some mountains.

679
00:46:14,738 --> 00:46:17,741
She sold a mountain,
then used the money for it.

680
00:46:19,943 --> 00:46:22,846
I didn't know that.

681
00:46:23,614 --> 00:46:27,785
First year, I peeked at her diary
then I found out about it.

682
00:46:29,887 --> 00:46:33,724
Although it was a third-rate university,
I thought I was accepted on my ability.

683
00:46:34,191 --> 00:46:35,692
I was very frustrated.

684
00:46:36,860 --> 00:46:38,228
I dropped out of there,

685
00:46:38,462 --> 00:46:43,333
studied very hard
and entered Totei University.

686
00:46:47,204 --> 00:46:48,071
I see.

687
00:46:49,840 --> 00:46:51,275
You have a rebellious spirit.

688
00:46:58,749 --> 00:47:00,617
Doctors are great.

689
00:47:01,418 --> 00:47:03,887
I realized that today.

690
00:47:05,489 --> 00:47:08,992
Right? Doctors are great.

691
00:47:09,593 --> 00:47:11,595
You are a great doctor, too.

692
00:47:12,162 --> 00:47:13,030
Yes.

693
00:47:15,599 --> 00:47:16,567
Keep doing your best.

694
00:47:17,334 --> 00:47:19,570
Let's both do our best.

695
00:47:21,205 --> 00:47:22,172
Yes, Dr. Ebina.

696
00:47:23,407 --> 00:47:24,474
Thank you so much.

697
00:47:24,875 --> 00:47:26,210
It's okay.

698
00:47:27,711 --> 00:47:28,879
Let's drink.

699
00:47:33,350 --> 00:47:34,251
Thank you.

700
00:47:37,020 --> 00:47:38,589
Excuse me.

701
00:47:39,823 --> 00:47:41,058
Here he comes.

702
00:47:41,124 --> 00:47:47,264
Thank you for employing Daimon
and Jonouchi from our agency.

703
00:47:47,898 --> 00:47:48,999
What is this concerning?

704
00:47:49,533 --> 00:47:50,534
Concerning?

705
00:47:52,603 --> 00:47:53,704
Here is a melon.

706
00:47:55,305 --> 00:47:56,607
The bill.

707
00:47:56,840 --> 00:47:57,708
Melon?

708
00:47:57,774 --> 00:48:00,143
You can't eat the melon.

709
00:48:00,878 --> 00:48:04,448
Let him look at the bill.

710
00:48:04,581 --> 00:48:08,385
He's online, connected to
our accounting department.

711
00:48:08,452 --> 00:48:10,520
Okay. Well...

712
00:48:11,488 --> 00:48:17,394
By the way, during this operation,
Daimon acted as a double.

713
00:48:17,761 --> 00:48:20,931
I'll carry this secret to the grave.

714
00:48:21,064 --> 00:48:23,233
So you raised the price.

715
00:48:25,035 --> 00:48:26,436
- Well.
- Go ahead.

716
00:48:28,205 --> 00:48:29,139
$200,000?

717
00:48:29,740 --> 00:48:30,941
This is a rip-off.

718
00:48:32,609 --> 00:48:34,945
That's a rip-off!

719
00:48:35,245 --> 00:48:36,346
Rip-off!

720
00:48:36,413 --> 00:48:39,583
Even if you say so,

721
00:48:39,650 --> 00:48:43,787
this is a reasonable price.

722
00:48:44,154 --> 00:48:45,822
We can't pay.

723
00:48:46,456 --> 00:48:48,058
We can't pay.

724
00:48:48,959 --> 00:48:50,761
- Is it okay? Well...
- Okay.

725
00:48:50,894 --> 00:48:52,296
That's what you mean. What?

726
00:48:55,699 --> 00:48:57,200
It's all right.

727
00:48:58,535 --> 00:48:59,836
We will transfer within this week.

728
00:49:00,103 --> 00:49:02,272
Thank you so much.

729
00:49:05,342 --> 00:49:06,209
$200,000.

730
00:49:17,154 --> 00:49:23,093
This manager is nice!

731
00:49:23,327 --> 00:49:24,494
Terrific!

732
00:49:27,965 --> 00:49:29,766
Bravo!

733
00:49:30,067 --> 00:49:32,169
Bravo!

734
00:49:32,970 --> 00:49:37,908
Bravo!

735
00:49:38,041 --> 00:49:40,811
"Reserved
Japan Doctors Club"

736
00:49:41,211 --> 00:49:42,279
I see.

737
00:49:42,746 --> 00:49:47,184
Freelance Michiko Daimon took over
from the middle of the surgery.

738
00:49:48,218 --> 00:49:51,588
The important thing is the method

739
00:49:51,989 --> 00:49:56,059
used in the operation.
It was proposed by...

740
00:49:56,994 --> 00:49:58,829
- What's his name?
- Ito.

741
00:49:59,830 --> 00:50:02,599
It was his idea.

742
00:50:03,333 --> 00:50:07,938
A great young surgeon of and from Totei.

743
00:50:08,505 --> 00:50:09,439
Yes.

744
00:50:09,940 --> 00:50:15,479
He has a promising future. Other facts
and circumstances don't matter.

745
00:50:16,980 --> 00:50:19,416
It's world news worthy.

746
00:50:20,550 --> 00:50:23,153
In a few days, give a press conference.

747
00:50:23,487 --> 00:50:24,354
Yes sir.

748
00:50:24,621 --> 00:50:25,722
Don't use that word.

749
00:50:26,423 --> 00:50:27,991
Certainly.

750
00:50:35,899 --> 00:50:40,003
Our young surgeon, Ryoji Ito

751
00:50:40,871 --> 00:50:44,975
from our Totei University Hospital,

752
00:50:45,509 --> 00:50:50,847
under the guidance of Deputy
Chief Surgeon Ebina, has become

753
00:50:51,314 --> 00:50:54,851
the first surgeon of his generation
in the world

754
00:50:56,186 --> 00:51:00,057
to perform this method.
And saved his mother's life.

755
00:51:03,193 --> 00:51:07,397
It may sound like bragging, but

756
00:51:07,864 --> 00:51:10,834
let me announce that

757
00:51:12,135 --> 00:51:14,905
a new star is born

758
00:51:15,238 --> 00:51:16,973
from Totei University Hospital.

759
00:51:22,212 --> 00:51:23,914
A star...

760
00:51:24,347 --> 00:51:27,350
He has something special.

761
00:51:27,684 --> 00:51:34,157
Let him introduce himself.

762
00:51:34,591 --> 00:51:35,525
Ito.

763
00:51:39,296 --> 00:51:41,264
You can tell them what we talked.

764
00:51:48,205 --> 00:51:51,141
Through this case,

765
00:51:51,708 --> 00:51:53,844
I realized that doctors are great.

766
00:51:55,545 --> 00:51:58,882
Now I know how much worth I am.

767
00:51:59,449 --> 00:52:01,685
Don't be humble.
Be proud of yourself.

768
00:52:04,387 --> 00:52:06,690
Therefore, today

769
00:52:10,861 --> 00:52:11,795
I will quit being

770
00:52:12,329 --> 00:52:13,263
a doctor.

771
00:52:13,830 --> 00:52:14,698
What?

772
00:52:16,566 --> 00:52:17,400
What?

773
00:52:20,504 --> 00:52:21,972
What's he talking?

774
00:52:22,706 --> 00:52:24,141
What's wrong with him?

775
00:52:24,641 --> 00:52:26,576
Is anything wrong with
the hospital system?

776
00:52:27,444 --> 00:52:29,179
No, not like that.

777
00:52:29,312 --> 00:52:32,716
My colleague's words hit me.

778
00:52:33,517 --> 00:52:35,485
Harassment? Crank?

779
00:52:35,552 --> 00:52:36,820
Bullying?

780
00:52:37,521 --> 00:52:38,722
There's nothing like that.

781
00:52:40,090 --> 00:52:42,659
Ebina.

782
00:52:43,727 --> 00:52:46,663
I won't give up.

783
00:52:49,432 --> 00:52:53,136
To be stubborn and mentally prepared
are totally different.

784
00:52:55,372 --> 00:52:56,206
And...

785
00:52:58,074 --> 00:53:01,278
I never fail.

786
00:53:06,550 --> 00:53:09,686
The words from Dr. Michiko Daimon
whom I respect.

787
00:53:11,321 --> 00:53:12,155
Daimon?

788
00:53:14,391 --> 00:53:17,827
Dr. Daimon performed most of
the operation.

789
00:53:20,964 --> 00:53:24,234
She saved my mother's life.

790
00:53:24,968 --> 00:53:26,336
He is not the surgeon?

791
00:53:26,536 --> 00:53:27,904
What is meant by that?

792
00:53:31,441 --> 00:53:37,147
If you aim to be a doctor,
everyone should emulate Dr. Daimon.

793
00:53:37,881 --> 00:53:42,786
It doesn't matter whether you're
a regular medical officer or freelance.

794
00:53:43,220 --> 00:53:44,821
Yes, I know.

795
00:53:45,088 --> 00:53:46,089
I...

796
00:53:46,790 --> 00:53:48,258
never fail.

797
00:53:49,092 --> 00:53:51,995
If I was a doctor, I'd want to
use those words.

798
00:53:52,295 --> 00:53:54,898
I should say that.

799
00:53:57,801 --> 00:54:00,770
But I can't say those words right now.

800
00:54:01,771 --> 00:54:03,173
I'm not mentally prepared.

801
00:54:06,776 --> 00:54:09,312
I realized who I am.

802
00:54:10,313 --> 00:54:11,681
Now I know for sure.

803
00:54:13,984 --> 00:54:18,922
All thanks to Dr. Daimon.

804
00:54:27,497 --> 00:54:28,765
Dr. Ito.

805
00:54:30,300 --> 00:54:32,369
- Uh-oh.
- Seriously?

806
00:54:36,339 --> 00:54:38,508
What is Dr. Daimon like?

807
00:54:39,709 --> 00:54:43,113
Please forget this press conference.

808
00:54:46,383 --> 00:54:47,384
Ebina.

809
00:54:49,052 --> 00:54:52,822
How are you going to pay for this?

810
00:54:54,224 --> 00:54:55,358
It's nice to be

811
00:54:58,662 --> 00:54:59,596
young.

812
00:55:01,831 --> 00:55:03,266
What did you say?

813
00:55:04,701 --> 00:55:05,635
What?

814
00:55:07,537 --> 00:55:08,505
Ebina.

815
00:55:12,575 --> 00:55:13,443
Ebina.

816
00:55:17,280 --> 00:55:19,316
Please say a few words.

817
00:55:21,184 --> 00:55:24,788
This was Totei University Hospital
the world's first to perform

818
00:55:24,888 --> 00:55:29,225
simultaneous resection of
the hepatopancreatic duodenum.

819
00:55:45,375 --> 00:55:48,645
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

820
00:55:50,380 --> 00:55:56,453
If it's not important
please come back later.

821
00:55:56,753 --> 00:56:00,357
I'm really upset right now.

822
00:56:06,162 --> 00:56:08,164
Someone else is more upset.

823
00:56:08,698 --> 00:56:10,400
Chairman Uchikanda.

824
00:56:17,640 --> 00:56:19,876
I've never known

825
00:56:23,413 --> 00:56:25,682
such humiliation.

826
00:56:35,458 --> 00:56:36,893
<i>In 2017</i>

827
00:56:37,594 --> 00:56:42,432
<i>the university medical system</i>
<i>regained its once-lost authority</i>

828
00:56:43,400 --> 00:56:49,172
<i>and the system on which lives depend</i>
<i>strayed away from what it should be.</i>

829
00:56:50,073 --> 00:56:52,976
The full amount for Michiko Daimon
is already paid.

830
00:56:55,278 --> 00:56:59,182
What a loose safe keeper.

831
00:56:59,249 --> 00:57:05,722
We'll report Kanbara Locum Doctor Agency
as a case of undue billing.

832
00:57:06,089 --> 00:57:08,291
I'm considering taking this to a trial.

833
00:57:11,261 --> 00:57:14,731
Michiko Daimon weakens this
organization and

834
00:57:15,398 --> 00:57:20,970
Chairman Uchikanda wishes to dismiss her.

835
00:57:21,971 --> 00:57:22,806
Yes sir.

836
00:57:24,274 --> 00:57:25,608
Don't use that word.

837
00:57:26,443 --> 00:57:27,610
You mean, "Yes sir"?

838
00:57:28,478 --> 00:57:29,579
No "Yes sir"?

839
00:57:29,712 --> 00:57:32,115
TAKOYAKI

840
00:57:32,882 --> 00:57:37,520
<i>In the midst of all this, doctors free</i>
<i>from any establishment emerged.</i>

841
00:57:37,921 --> 00:57:41,624
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

842
00:57:41,758 --> 00:57:42,792
Thank you.

843
00:57:43,726 --> 00:57:45,829
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

844
00:57:46,396 --> 00:57:50,366
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

845
00:57:51,201 --> 00:57:56,539
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

846
00:57:58,608 --> 00:58:01,211
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

847
00:58:02,011 --> 00:58:05,515
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

848
00:58:05,682 --> 00:58:10,520
I heard the young surgeon Ito
quit being a doctor.

849
00:58:11,054 --> 00:58:13,223
Not the hospital?
Quit being a doctor?

850
00:58:13,289 --> 00:58:14,123
Yeah.

851
00:58:14,257 --> 00:58:17,327
He was the best of
the four young surgeons.

852
00:58:17,560 --> 00:58:19,329
What is he going to do?

853
00:58:19,596 --> 00:58:21,931
He wants to become a musician.

854
00:58:22,298 --> 00:58:23,833
Musician?

855
00:58:24,267 --> 00:58:26,336
He was in a band when he was a student.

856
00:58:26,803 --> 00:58:28,905
He plays the bass guitar.

857
00:58:29,138 --> 00:58:29,973
Bass guitar?

858
00:58:30,206 --> 00:58:31,541
Bass...

859
00:58:31,608 --> 00:58:34,511
A bassist is not versatile...

860
00:58:34,577 --> 00:58:37,447
They can only play bass and nothing else.

861
00:58:37,514 --> 00:58:39,716
Yeah, that's right.

862
00:58:39,816 --> 00:58:41,985
The bassist isn't in the spotlight.

863
00:58:42,051 --> 00:58:42,952
Yeah, I know.

864
00:58:43,019 --> 00:58:43,887
Too plain.

865
00:58:43,953 --> 00:58:45,855
- A sober sound.
- Yeah.

866
00:58:45,955 --> 00:58:48,191
The sound's like this.

867
00:58:54,631 --> 00:58:56,132
It's not true.

868
00:58:57,867 --> 00:59:00,403
What's wrong with you?

869
00:59:00,503 --> 00:59:01,671
I didn't say anything.

870
00:59:01,771 --> 00:59:03,006
Did I make him mad?

871
00:59:03,106 --> 00:59:04,207
I'm not mad.

872
00:59:04,340 --> 00:59:05,275
You look angry.

873
00:59:05,341 --> 00:59:06,576
It's normal.

874
00:59:07,210 --> 00:59:08,878
That's not normal.

875
00:59:09,412 --> 00:59:11,381
Corrupt doctor!

876
00:59:11,514 --> 00:59:12,782
Second opinion?

877
00:59:12,916 --> 00:59:15,285
- He's my patient.
- Name your price.

878
00:59:15,418 --> 00:59:16,653
I'll operate.

879
00:59:16,719 --> 00:59:19,422
Fail intentionally and blame it on Daimon?

880
00:59:19,522 --> 00:59:21,057
- Sutures.
- I decline.

881
00:59:21,190 --> 00:59:23,426
- What?
- The operation isn't finished.
